# Security Review Checklist

Use for security-focused review across backend, expiry-job, and frontend. Reference `docs/security.md`.

## Secrets & deployment

- [ ] No credentials, tokens, or PII in code, logs, or commits
- [ ] Env vars documented in `.env.example`; production secrets not in repo
- [ ] AWS identifiers only via env

## Authentication & authorization

- [ ] All non-login routes require valid JWT
- [ ] No auth bypass for job endpoints
- [ ] Resource `:id` routes don't assume ID secrecy

## Input & output

- [ ] All inputs validated; enums whitelisted
- [ ] Error messages don't leak stack traces or internal details in production
- [ ] SQL injection prevented (parameterized queries only)

## Data integrity

- [ ] Soft delete preserved; audit chain (`renewedFromId`) not broken
- [ ] Status cannot be tampered via client
- [ ] Transactions used for multi-row operations (renewal, cascade)

## Transport & CORS

- [ ] HTTPS enforced outside local dev
- [ ] CORS restricted to known origins

## Output format

Categorize as **critical** / **high** / **medium** / **low**. Critical = must fix before merge.
